<title>USA: St. Francis to buy back 10 pct of shares.</title>
<headline>St. Francis to buy back 10 pct of shares.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Francis Capital Corp said Thursday its board approved a new share repurchase program of up to 10 percent of the company's 5.4 million outstanding shares.</p>
<p>The bank holding company said it completed the buyback of five percent of its outstanding common shares. That program began in July, 1996 and resulted in the purchase of 282,945 shares at an average price of $25.75 per share.</p>
<p>It said the new repurchase program will start November 11 and involve buying 538,100 shares over a 12-month period.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
